* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-loop-bandwidth-pm (issue #27, Part of #16)
* Linearised open-loop AC sweep of the type-II charge-pump PLL, built around
* the REAL, unmodified `loop_filter` subckt (frozen in
* ../netlist-snapshots/loop_filter.spice), so the loop's own impedance term
* comes from the actual `rppd` and `cap_cmomi` compact models at a real
* process corner and temperature -- not from a textbook R-C expression.
*
* `../testbench/run.sh` substitutes @CORNER_RES@ (cornerRES.lib section),
* @TEMP@ (degC), @KD@ (charge-pump gain Icp/2*pi, A/rad), @KV@ (VCO gain
* 2*pi*Kvco, rad/s per V), @INVN@ (1/N) per ../corners/matrix.md, and
* @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (resolved filesystem path -- ngspice's `.lib`/`.include`
* parser does not expand shell/OS environment variables, issue #44).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS REAL HERE AND WHAT IS BEHAVIOURAL
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* REAL (extracted compact models, swept over their own corners):
*   - the loop filter's R1 (`rppd`) and C1/C2 (`cap_cmomi`), instantiated
*     from the frozen design export with no edit.
* BEHAVIOURAL (linearised small-signal stand-ins, each with its own numeric
* value taken from a REAL measurement recorded elsewhere in this repo):
*   - the phase detector + charge pump, as a transconductance @KD@ =
*     Icp/(2*pi) A/rad. Icp comes from
*     ../../sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim/corners/results.csv (a real DC sweep of
*     the committed `cp` subckt), not from an assumption.
*   - the VCO, as an ideal phase integrator of gain @KV@ = 2*pi*Kvco. Kvco
*     comes from ../../sg13cmos5l-vco-kvco-table/corners/results.csv (a real
*     PVT-cornered transient sweep of the committed `vco` subckt).
*   - the feedback divider, as a memoryless 1/N gain (@INVN@). This is the
*     standard continuous-time approximation and is exactly why the
*     f_c < f_ref/10 sampled-loop ceiling exists as a separate criterion --
*     see ../records/RECORD-001 "What this does not bound".
* No transistor-level closed-loop transient is run here; ../records/RECORD-001
* states plainly which spec rows that leaves unbounded.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.include @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include loop_filter_snap.spice

Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

* 1 rad of AC phase error into the phase detector
Vpe pe 0 dc 0 ac 1

* Phase detector + charge pump: Icp/(2*pi) amperes per radian, injected into
* the filter node.
Gcp 0 vctrl pe 0 @KD@

* The real, unmodified loop filter (VCTRL, VSS)
XLF vctrl 0 loop_filter

* VCO as an ideal phase integrator: 1 F on `vph` makes V(vph) the running
* integral of @KV@ * V(vctrl), i.e. a transfer of @KV@/s rad per volt.
* Rleak only keeps the node DC-defined; its own pole sits at 1.6e-16 Hz.
Gvco 0 vph vctrl 0 @KV@
Cint vph 0 1
Rleak vph 0 1e15

* Feedback divider: memoryless 1/N
Ediv fb 0 vph 0 @INVN@

.control
ac dec 200 10 1e9
let mag_ol = mag(v(fb))
let ph_ol = 180*cph(v(fb))/pi
wrdata ac.dat mag_ol ph_ol
.endc
.end
